   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch1/q2",
   "question": "<p>The infinite series <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S\"></span> are defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C=\\cos\\theta+\\frac12\\cos5\\theta+\\frac14\\cos9\\theta+\\frac18\\cos13\\theta+\\dots\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S=\\sin\\theta+\\frac12\\sin5\\theta+\\frac14\\sin9\\theta+\\frac18\\sin13\\theta+\\dots\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that the series <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S\"></span> are both convergent,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C+\\mathrm i\\mathrm S=\\frac{2\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}}{2-\\mathrm e^{4\\mathrm i\\theta}}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li><p>Hence show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S=\\frac{4\\sin\\theta+2\\sin3\\theta}{5-4\\cos4\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
