   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch1/q4",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|z|&lt;1\"></span>, write down the sum of the infinite series</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"1+z+z^2+z^3+\\dots\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=\\dfrac12(\\cos\\theta+\\mathrm i\\sin\\theta)\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><p>use the answer to part (a), and de Moivre's theorem or otherwise, to prove that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12\\sin\\theta+\\frac14\\sin2\\theta+\\frac18\\sin3\\theta+\\dots=\\frac{2\\sin\\theta}{5-4\\cos\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>show that the sum of the infinite series <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+z+z^2+z^3+\\dots\"></span> cannot be purely imaginary, giving a reason for your answer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
