   "id": "pmt/pure-core-2/ch1/q6",
   "question": "<p>A complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z\"></span> has modulus 1 and argument <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"z^n+\\frac{1}{z^n}=2\\cos n\\theta,\\qquad n\\in\\mathbb Z^+\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li><p>Hence, show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos^4\\theta=\\frac18(\\cos4\\theta+4\\cos2\\theta+3)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
