   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><p>Use de Moivre's theorem to show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sin^5\\theta\\equiv a\\sin5\\theta+b\\sin3\\theta+c\\sin\\theta\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}\\sin^5\\theta\\,\\mathrm d\\theta=\\frac{53}{480}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
